PICS 0
BACnet Protocol Implementation Conformance Statement
Vendor Name: "Chipkin Automation Systems"
Product Name: "CAS BACnet Stack Example - B-EC"
Product Model Number: "CAS BACnet Stack Example - B-EC"
Product Description: "A BACnet/IP elevator controller built on the CAS BACnet Stack. It reports what an elevator installation (an Elevator Group, a Lift and an Escalator) is doing, the same object family as the B-EM example, and also accepts commands: WriteProperty and WritePropertyMultiple to three commandable outputs and to the Elevator Group's Landing_Call_Control (a landing call is served by a simulated lift car), TimeSynchronization and ReinitializeDevice. It supports SubscribeCOV and SubscribeCOVPropertyMultiple, generates intrinsic event notifications (CHANGE_OF_STATE on the Lift's Passenger_Alarm, FAULT_LISTED on its Fault_Signals), accepts AcknowledgeAlarm, answers GetEventInformation, handles DeviceCommunicationControl, and is discoverable by Who-Is and Who-Has (it can also initiate a Who-Is). It is a tutorial for implementers of the B-EC profile."

BACnet Standardized Device Profiles Supported:
{
B-EC - BACnet Elevator Controller
}

